<title>USA: BSkyB seen planning film division - report.</title>
<headline>BSkyB seen planning film division - report.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Sky Broadcasting is said to be planning a new division BSkyB Films, to invest in film production and possibly build a studio in Britain, Daily Variety said on Friday.</p>
<p>BSkyB would not confirm the plan, the paper said, but the satellite broadcaster was said to be in discussions with News Corp's 20th Century Fox over how to proceed. News Corp, Fox's parent, owns 40 percent of BSkyB.</p>
<p>Such a move would complement BSkyB's new commitment to producing more original television programming, Variety said. Traditionally, BSkyB acquired the vast bulk of its programming and placed little emphasis on production, the paper said.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
